            <ArticleTitle>Use of GlideScope® in adults: an overview.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>342-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper is an overview of the literature concerning the &quot;know how&quot; of the GlideScope® use in adults. We summarized the main evidences of the last 10 years with particular attention to experts' suggestions about clinical practice of the GlideScope®, noticing matters still debated on GlideScope® use. We used PubMed to search publications from January 2003 to June 2013 using the search terms &quot;GlideScope&quot;, &quot;video laryngoscope&quot; and &quot;videolaryngoscopy&quot;. These publications were searched manually or references to further publication not identified using PubMed. All works that made a point worth including were cited in the discussion. Our research confirms the value of GlideScope® use in airway management and highlights the debate about the use of videolaryngoscopes in routine cases and the operators who may use them in clinical practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
